do_1 = "At services/agent/sdk/python/layerx_sdk/x402_http.py:634 and :642, separate the settlement extension from the submitted proof using a settlement-specific parser; validate landingBlockHeight as a canonical bounded hex quantity and landingBlockHash as a 32-byte hex value, require the pair together when present and bind it to independently authenticated committed evidence, then pass only the validated receipt members to the existing proof verifier; preserve the strict submitted-proof schema at :226, both proof verifications at :649, transaction and payer binding at :651, and commitment downgrade refusal at :646, following decision 2570 at spec/layerx-merge/spec.kvx:8535."
do_2 = "Extend the real paymentPeer in services/platform/middleware/conformance/pay6/peers.mjs:42 with a committed resource and its fixture information, using the existing recorded committed receipt and trusted validator evidence from services/platform/middleware/seller/test/committed-fixture.mjs:5; obtain PAYMENT-RESPONSE from real SellerMiddleware.handle through the HTTP route at peers.mjs:68, retaining the existing receipted resource and preserving the seller header unchanged."
do_3 = "Add test_typescript_settlement_metadata_round_trip to services/platform/middleware/conformance/pay6/test_http.py beside HttpTests at :21; exercise Python BuyerMiddleware.fetch through the real TypeScript seller's 402 and paid HTTP responses for receipted and committed fixtures, then capture the unchanged response and assert its canonical receipt, digest, transaction and resource; assert rejection of either landing field alone, malformed height or hash, references mismatching authenticated evidence, unknown extension members, substituted proof members, invalid signatures or pins, missing or invalid trusted commitment evidence and committed-to-receipted downgrades; metadata alone must never establish committed finality, and submitted proofs must still reject settlement-only members."
